{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "5c0976f0-d8f0-8298-8af7-fc42bd390858",
  "created_at": "2026-02-27T10:52:41-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Manuel Medeiros",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:49:53-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:49:56-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Morning, Kevin. Manuel Medeiros here. Well, I think it's still morning. My bin and I are having a disagreement."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. It's just about eleven, so you're still good. What's going on with the bin?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:09-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So I put out my recycling this week like always, and the truck came, but the bin's still sitting there full. There's a tag hanging on the handle that says rejected. That's all it says. Rejected."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:21-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, rejected tag. Did it have a box checked off, or a reason written on it anywhere? Usually there's a little list."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:29-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me look. [pause] Hang on, I've got it in my hand. There's a few boxes. Um, one's got a check by it, I think it says contaminated. Or maybe that's the one above it. I can't tell, it's kind of smudged."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:43-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Contaminated usually means something in there that doesn't belong. Plastic bags, food stuff, greasy pizza boxes, that kind of thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:50:50-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, but I thought bags were fine? I bag everything so it doesn't blow around. Wait, are the bags the problem or the stuff inside the bags?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Bags are usually the problem. Recyclables go in loose. Bagged stuff gets treated as trash, so they leave it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Huh. So loose. Not in a bag, not in a box either?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:12-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Loose in the bin. Cardboard flattened is fine, just not inside a bag."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:17-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I had that backwards. Sorry, there's a little clicking on my phone, hopefully you can hear me alright."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:24-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear it, a soft click every few seconds, but you're coming through fine. Let me get this down. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "160 Old Beach Road, down by Easton's Beach."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "One sixty Old Beach Road, bin rejected, bagged recyclables. Got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:40-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So when's the next pickup? Is it next Friday, or is recycling every other week? I never remember which one I'm on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:48-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me pull up your route. [pause] Okay, looks like it's every other week for recycling, so you'd be due the Friday after next, not next Friday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:51:58-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wait, so not next week. Two weeks from today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, two weeks from today. So take the bags out, put it all in loose, and set it out that morning or the night before."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:11-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And the stuff that's already in there, I just dump the bags out into the bin?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:17-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, empty the bags into the bin and toss the bags in the trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I think I've got it. Loose, two weeks. Unless it's the other one, the trash is weekly, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Trash is weekly, recycling every other. You've got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:33-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. Thanks, Kevin. I'll try again and see if it sticks this time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-27T10:52:38-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. Have a good weekend."
    }
  ],
